  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 157 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nThursday...Upper ridging will persist across the Central U.S. with \ntroughing across the western U.S. with a closed low moving inland. \nSoutherly winds will increase to 15 to 25 mph across the west with \nhighs 75 to 80 and partly cloudy skies. \n\nThursday night through Friday...The upper trough is forecast to move \ninto the Rockies. A slight chance for showers Friday. Windy Friday \narea wide, at 20 to 30 mph with local gusts to 45 mph. Highs \nFriday 75 to 84. \n\nFriday night through Saturday night, increased chances for showers \nand a few thunderstorms Friday night as a cold front arrives in the \nwest late Friday night. The main upper trough lifts through the \nregion Saturday into Sunday and interacts with the front. The GFS \nremains faster with the upper trough passage, while the ECMWF is \nslower and stalls the front over the area into Sunday. Consensus is \nfor the best potential for showers to be across the southeastern \nhalf of the area. Highs cooling into the upper 50s to mid 60s \nSaturday.\n\nSunday and Monday...lingering slight chance for showers, mainly \nsouth and east, as the upper trough weakens and moves east. Highs \neach day more seasonable in the upper 50s to near 65.",
